course: dictionary
lesson: 1424
title: Carmaker: a company that makes cars
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A carmaker is a company, not a person. It designs cars, which means it plans how they will look and work, and it builds them, which means it makes them in factories.
explain: Read the sentence: «The three-point seat belt was invented at Volvo in 1959, and the company let other carmakers use it for free.» Volvo is the company, and the other carmakers are other car companies. The word company is a clue that carmakers are businesses.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «The company let other car companies use it for free» still makes sense, so carmaker means a car company. Big carmakers include Ford, Toyota and Volkswagen.
fact: A carmaker is a company that designs and builds cars.
fact: Examples of carmakers are Ford, Toyota and Volkswagen.
fact: «Carmaker» is a noun. Its plural is carmakers.
fact: In «The three-point seat belt was invented at Volvo in 1959», Volvo is a carmaker.
fact: In geography, carmakers provide factories and jobs. In maths, they appear in problems about how many cars are produced.
exercise: What is a carmaker? | *A company that designs and builds cars | A road for lorries | A person who drives a taxi | A shop that sells sweets
exercise: In «the company let other carmakers use it for free», who are the other carmakers? | People who sell cars in a showroom | Drivers who share their seat belts | Children who play with toy cars | *Other car companies that build cars
exercise: Which of these is a carmaker? | A bus driver | A petrol station | A bicycle shop | *Volkswagen
test: Ford and Toyota are examples of what? | Sweet shops | *Carmakers | Bus stops | Pilots
test: Which word means a company that designs and builds cars? | Carpet | *Carmaker | Carrier | Carpenter
exam: Carmakers, such as Ford, Toyota or Volkswagen, do what? | Grow food on farms | *Design and build cars | Sell only bicycles | Teach maths in schools
